  "story": {
    "who": "Maren Karlson, who according to an ArtReview review is German-born and based in Los Angeles, paints from newspaper images in a distorted, digitally adjusted way. ArtReview has reviewed this Soft Opening show.",
    "now": "ArtReview explains that the title LAG is the ending of the name Axel Springer Verlag, the final three letters. The review links the show to events that led to the Red Army Faction being founded, and says it also includes two photographs alongside the paintings.",
    "vibe": "ArtReview describes a spare white room where each painting sits in a low alcove raised about 25 centimetres off the concrete. The reviewer says the greyish works read like footnotes.",
    "worth_knowing": [
      "Each painting is set in a low alcove built for the show, about 25cm above the floor, says ArtReview.",
      "The photographs use articles photocopied from the Springer Verlag public archive, according to ArtReview."
    ],
